The graph compares two monthly repayments on a reducing balance loan of $\$30\,000$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{loanblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{loanred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{loangrid}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=10cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,xmin=0,xmax=120,ymin=0,ymax=32000,xtick={0,20,40,60,80,100,120},ytick={0,10000,20000,30000},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,/pgf/number format/fixed},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={Months},ylabel={Balance owing (\$)},ylabel style={at={(axis description cs:-0.28,0.5)},anchor=south},grid=major,grid style={draw=loangrid},axis line style={black},samples=100,clip=false]
\addplot[thick,loanblue,domain=0:110.411]{45000-15000*exp(x*ln(1.01))};
\addplot[thick,loanred,dashed,domain=0:51.338]{75000-45000*exp(x*ln(1.01))};
\node[anchor=west,text=loanblue,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] at (axis cs:63,20000) {\$450 per month};
\node[anchor=west,text=loanred,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] at (axis cs:24,10000) {\$750 per month};
\end{axis}
\path[use as bounding box] ([xshift=-4mm]current bounding box.south west) rectangle (current bounding box.north east);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Read each loan term to the nearest $10$ months. Use these estimates to estimate how much less is repaid at $\$750$ per month.
